            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0325" n="253" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg253"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5869/236.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The French Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >French Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: My Government has just
                    advised me that the last day on which the commercial arrangements recently
                    denounced <pb facs="0326" n="254" xml:id="pg254"/> by the United States
                    Government can be applied happening to be a Sunday, the necessary arrangements
                    have been made to keep the French customhouse open on that day.</p>
                <p>I have, in consequence, the honor to inform your excellency that American imports
                    will enjoy the benefits of the present order for products arrived and entered in
                    France on the 31st of this month.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, etc,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jusserand.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
